  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "In a 9x9 inch baking dish, combine the pork and beans, brown sugar, onion, ketchup, mustard, Worcestershire sauce and vinegar and season with salt and pepper to taste. Top with the bacon slices.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake at 350 degrees F (175 degrees C) for 1 hour, or until sauce is thickened and bacon is cooked.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "These beans are great! I only used 1/4 cup each of brown sugar and ketchup, so there was no problem with it being \"runny\". I also cooked 4 slices of bacon then chopped it and mixed it in. That way I could use more bacon, but keep the grease out.",
      "group": null
    }
